# `total` is reached from outside, so nothing is proven of `rows`: the tests of the helper's guard stand in front of its copy, and where one fails the slow version is called with the arrow.
# That call only borrows the arrow (Link: the helper only calls what arrives there), and nobody has the scope of `sum` so far: so a scope is made there, out of what the state holds, the arrow over it, and `sum` is read back behind the call.
# The first scope then has no reader on any way: no store is left in a turn, and the one allocation stands in the rare block. Behind the read nobody has that cell, by the proof that let it be lent: it is handed back there.
# OPTIONS: check=Validate
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK: Branch {{*}}notTaken [[slow]]()
# CHECK: [[slow]]() frequency=Rare:
# CHECK-NEXT: [[copy]]: {{*}} = NewObject {{*}}fields=[0]
# CHECK-NEXT: [[lent]]: {{*}} = NewClosure [[copy]] {{*}}loan=ToFunctionEntered
# CHECK: = CallDirect {{*}}role=SlowBody
# CHECK-NEXT: = GetEnvironmentField [[copy]]
# CHECK-NEXT: ReleaseEnvironment [[copy]]
# RUN(STORES): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# STORES-NOT: PutEnvironmentField
# Whoever may keep the arrow shares the scope with what the maker writes later: a call by value of what nobody knows takes the arrow over the one scope, which is made and written as ever and read behind the call.
# RUN(STUB): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# STUB-LABEL: code f4:Body
# STUB: [[scope]]: {{*}} = NewObject
# STUB: PutEnvironmentField [[scope]]
# STUB: = NewClosure [[scope]]
# STUB: = Call
# STUB: = GetEnvironmentField [[scope]]
# RUN(ONE): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# ONE-NOT: fields=[0]
# A throw in the borrowed call leads to a handler that reads the memory of the first scope: under a handler the first scope itself is lent.
# RUN(CAUGHT): walk f6 mechanisms=all
# CAUGHT-LABEL: code f6:Body
# CAUGHT-NOT: fields=[0]
# RUN(WITHHELD): walk f2 mechanisms=all-EscapeAnalysis
# WITHHELD: PutEnvironmentField
